Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 00:37:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(a11y): add WCAG matrix, scoring, and Remedy review
 UI to Project Accessibility
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extends the Project Accessibility tab from the checkbox matrix into a WCAG
conformance view driven by scan results.

- accessibilityScore.ts extracts the scoring out of the component:
  computeA11yScore over the manual checkbox matrix, and
  computeWcagProjectSummary which aggregates per-page WCAG summaries across
  the project. The score denominator deliberately counts only pass/fail
  criteria — manual-review and not-tested criteria are reported separately
  rather than being folded in as failures, so an unreviewed project reads as
  "not scored" (null) instead of 0%. Unit tests cover both.

- types/a11y.ts describes the stored review shape: criterion status,
  applicability, per-finding evidence, and DOJ exception records.

- ProjectAccessibility.jsx gains the WCAG matrix, a Remedy health indicator,
  per-section scan, and a fix workflow that previews an HTML diff before
  anything is applied. Apply is only offered after a preview, and carries the
  preview hash back so the server can reject a stale one.

Tests run under vitest, matching the existing client suite.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
